window.docContents[46].resolve({"/What-a-p-adic-L-function-should-be/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--What-a-p-adic-L-function-should-be":{"contents":"This chapter motivates the definition and study of -adic -functions. We\nbegin with the classical complex -functions, recall how special values encode\narithmetic, and then lean slowly towards the -adic world. The running example\n— and the central object of these notes — is the Riemann zeta function. The\nchapter closes by fixing the interpolation property that the Kubota–Leopoldt\n-adic -function  must satisfy; constructing such an object is\nthe goal of the next several chapters.\n\nThroughout,  is a fixed prime and  ranges over rational primes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"An introduction to p-adic L-functions — Lean blueprint","header":"2. What a p-adic L-function should be","id":"/What-a-p-adic-L-function-should-be/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--What-a-p-adic-L-function-should-be"}});